's request ('a tuner for all four colours on white, same original hues just sat and brightness adjustments, normalise to the chroma values that we store') - ITS OUTPUTS ARE OFFERS, NOT RULINGS. ANY REVISION OF THESE TWO HEXES OFF THAT TUNER WOULD BE A NEW RULING, NOT AN AMENDMENT OF THIS ONE. ||| SUPERSEDED IN PART BY s168-D5 (#168, same window, post-wrap) - BY ADDITION: NOTHING ABOVE IS REWRITTEN OR TRIMMED, it stands as the record of what #168 and #168-A believed. WHAT s168-D5 SUPERSEDES IS THE LIGHT HEXES OF THE GRAPHIC RUNG, AND ONLY THOSE. Dave took the FORWARD CLAUSE immediately above at its word, ruled off reviews/TUNER-168-graphic-light-legs-v1.html ('ink this will do'), and so this is a NEW RULING, not an amendment. SUPERSEDED FROM THIS RULING, quoted: 'the LIGHT leg is the ruled TEXT red #DA1A00' -> now #F3543E; 'the LIGHT leg is the ruled TEXT green #137F3C' -> now #57A369; 'the LIGHT leg is now #3F6FB5, the picker candidate Dave named 'desaturated'' -> now #6893D3. rag/warning-graphic LIGHT #C58900 is UNCHANGED IN VALUE and was re-ratified by eye against the tuner spread. WHAT OF THIS RULING STILL STANDS UNTOUCHED: all four DARK legs; the rung SHAPE, JOB and SCOPE; the UNRATIFIED rung name; and the open dark-leg $note contrast dispute. #DA1A00 and #137F3C are retired AS GRAPHIC LEGS ONLY - they remain the ruled INK/TEXT values on rag/error-ink and rag/success-ink, which s168-D5 does not touch.
