  ▸ s168-D5 — RULED #168 (2026-08-13, Dave): THE FOUR GRAPHIC LIGHT LEGS ARE RE-SEATED OFF THE TUNER. Dave ruled live, post-wrap, off reviews/TUNER-168-graphic-light-legs-v1.html, verbatim: "ink this will do". HIS EXPORT, QUOTED IN FULL AND VERBATIM: "### TUNER #168-A - four graphic LIGHT legs on white (OFFERS, not rulings) / Space: OKLCH. Hue LOCKED per leg. Chroma reference: MEAN of settled pair, C 0.1796. rag/error-graphic #DA1A00 -> **#F3543E** (L .659 C .1985 H 30.72, 3.415:1 PASS) - rag/warning-graphic **#C58900 unchanged** (3.021:1 PASS) - rag/success-graphic #137F3C -> **#57A369** (3.067:1 PASS) - rag/information-graphic #3F6FB5 -> **#6893D3** (3.133:1 PASS). 'A revision taken off this page is a NEW RULING, not an amendment of s168-D4.'" SO, THE RULED LIGHT LEGS OF THE GRAPHIC RUNG (mono base store, s167-D1 scope) ARE NOW: rag/error-graphic light = #F3543E; rag/warning-graphic light = #C58900 (VALUE UNCHANGED, STATUS RE-RATIFIED at this sitting - it was already Dave's ruled pick at #168-A and he re-judged it against the tuner spread and held it); rag/success-graphic light = #57A369; rag/information-graphic light = #6893D3. THREE VALUES CHANGE, ONE IS STATUS-ONLY. SUPERSESSION, BY ADDITION, NOT BY REWRITING: this ruling supersedes ONLY THE LIGHT HEXES seated under s168-D4 and its #168-A amendment. Superseded verbatim from s168-D4/#168-A, quoted so the change is legible: the light legs seated there were "the LIGHT leg is the ruled TEXT red #DA1A00" (error), "the LIGHT leg is the ruled TEXT green #137F3C" (success), and "the LIGHT leg is now #3F6FB5, the picker candidate Dave named 'desaturated'" (information). Those three hexes cease to be the graphic rung's light values. WHAT IS NOT SUPERSEDED AND EXPLICITLY STANDS: (a) ALL FOUR DARK LEGS - #CC4333, #C58900, #4A9568, #2674DC - UNTOUCHED; Dave's "I'm happy with the current colours in dark mode" is not reopened; (b) the RUNG SHAPE, its JOB (R-D3 wording, "chart series, standalone marks"), and its SCOPE (mono base store only per s167-D1; legacy and console/supercharge declare the rung ABSENT); (c) the rung NAME '-graphic' remains a DECLARED DEFAULT, STILL UNRATIFIED - this ruling does not name it; (d) the dark-leg $note contrast dispute (3.66:1 vs 3.42:1 on #CC4333) is STILL an open residual, untouched. RETIREMENT, NEVER DELETION: #DA1A00 and #137F3C are retired AS GRAPHIC LEGS ONLY - they REMAIN THE RULED INK/TEXT VALUES elsewhere (rag/error-ink light and rag/success-ink light, s144-D1/s151-D1/s155-D1), which this ruling does NOT touch. #3F6FB5 is retired as a graphic leg outright (it was never an ink value). MEASURED FIRST-HAND AT THIS SITTING, not trusted from the export - WCAG 2.x relative-luminance ratio on #FFFFFF: #F3543E = 3.415:1, #C58900 = 3.021:1, #57A369 = 3.067:1, #6893D3 = 3.133:1. All four clear dv-016 (>=3:1); NONE of them is text-grade (all below 4.5) and none is claimed to be - the rung is a GRAPHIC rung and the ink rungs carry text. NOTE THE DIRECTION OF TRAVEL: the three changed legs move DOWN in contrast (5.086 -> 3.415, 5.086 -> 3.067, 5.057 -> 3.133) because the tuner's job was to normalise chroma and lift lightness; this is a DELIBERATE, EYE-RULED trade of text-grade headroom for chromatic strength on the graphic rung, and it is legal because dv-016 is the rung's governing threshold. MEASURED RESIDUAL, DECLARED NOT FIXED: the export's stated chroma reference ("normalise to C 0.1796") is NOT achieved by three of the four hexes - measured OKLCH chroma is red 0.1986, green 0.1151, blue 0.1071, amber 0.1404. Only the red is near the stated target; green and blue sit well under it, almost certainly because C 0.1796 at those hues and lightnesses is outside the sRGB gamut and the tuner clipped. HUE LOCK HOLDS within rounding (red 30.72->30.82, green 150.06->149.89, blue 257.85->258.13). THE HEXES ARE WHAT DAVE RULED AND THE HEXES ARE WHAT IS SEATED - the chroma-normalisation NARRATIVE is an unproven description of them, not a constraint they satisfy. Dave's to reopen if the description mattered.
      status: RULED #168 (post-wrap, second post-wrap action), ENACTED AND MEASURED IN THE SAME WINDOW. The three changed light hexes are seated in knowledge/tokens/semantic-colour.json (textual), knowledge/tokens/palettes/rag/mono.json (round-trip byte-identical proof taken BEFORE writing), and the mono LIGHT block of knowledge/canon/canon.css (textual - gen_canon_tokens.py was NOT run), and re-projected into the Chart-bar snippet via gen_snippet_tokens.py. Dark legs, rung shape, rung scope and the unratified rung NAME are all untouched. OPEN RESIDUALS CARRIED FORWARD, unchanged by this ruling: (1) the rung name '-graphic' is a declared default, UNRATIFIED, Dave's to name; (2) the dark-leg $note contrast dispute (3.66:1 vs 3.42:1 on #CC4333) is unresolved; (3) NEW at this sitting - the chroma-normalisation narrative in Dave's export is not satisfied by three of the four hexes (see says), DECLARED not fixed. The tuner page's own clause is honoured: this is a NEW RULING, not an amendment of s168-D4.
      evidence: chat #168 2026-08-13 (live) - Dave verbatim, post-wrap, ruling off the tuner: 'ink this will do'; FIRM
