  ▸ s191-D2 — RULED Non-repo artefacts: home-or-declare (the W-31 rule) (2026-08-16, Dave): Memory hooks naming artefacts that legally live outside the repo are handled by HOME-OR-DECLARE, never left falsely STALE. (a) An artefact that CAN live in the repo is HOMED there — render.py moves to knowledge/_render/render.py as the canonical template the sandbox copies; the runbook copies, never retypes. (b) An artefact that CANNOT live in the repo (the consolidate-memory skill, installed in the Claude app's plugin cache) is DECLARED in the hook file with an adjacent marker: backticked path followed by (NON-REPO: <where it actually lives>) — the WHERE is mandatory. The grader (_gardener.py derive_probe_from_file) drops declared tokens from repo claims; a hook whose every path is declared non-repo grades UNPROVABLE with the declaration as evidence — honestly unverifiable, not stale.
