  ▸ s216-D1 — RULED THEME PUBLISHING: THE DELIVERABLE IS MINTED, DEV-READY, THEME-SPECIFIC CODE — ADR-0011 AMENDED WITH A PUBLISH TIER, NOT REVERSED (2026-08-22, Dave): The published deliverable per theme is dev-ready, theme-specific code: a set of primitives wired to a stylesheet, consumable as-is. Mechanism (delegated to conductor, Dave confirmed 'lets go with your recommendation'): authoring stays exactly as ADR-0011 ruled — one store, override sets, never a hand-managed fork — and a MINT step (s200-D1 discipline) compiles store + overrides into a self-contained per-theme stylesheet (e.g. console.compiled.css): every value concrete, primitives as custom properties at the top, components wired below, zero cross-theme machinery in the file. NOTED FOR THE FUTURE, not ruled: if added themes ever need STRUCTURAL divergence (different markup, not different values), hand-forking becomes a live option — Dave: 'not now though, worth noting the potential for this in the future'.
