  ▸ s217-D3 — RULED BENTO ROLES — DASHBOARD / BROCHUREWARE / GALLERY DECIDE RADIUS PLACEMENT, SPACING AND SQUARING; REFINES s217-D2, NOT REVERSED (2026-08-23, Dave): A bento instance carries a ROLE, and the role decides where radius and spacing sit (console named as the example because its radius token is non-zero; the grammar is identical in all four themes, radius simply resolves to 0 where the theme says square). DASHBOARD (sectioned app, bento-of-bentos): the theme radius sits on each inner bento's CONTAINER (the s217-D2 model), tiles inside at 1px spacing. BROCHUREWARE (sectioned marketing page): the tiles THEMSELVES carry the radius and the spacing. GALLERY (page-level, photography): tiles carry radius and spacing like brochureware, and the squaring pass RELAXES — orphans are acceptable, the requirement is only an appropriate layout for portrait and landscape images. SQUARING PASS RATIFIED for dashboard and brochureware roles (Dave: 'is very cool', with gallery exempted in the same breath). GALLERY ADDITIONS: more generous caption space (ruled); and a TRIAL, NOT RULED - keylines dropped entirely, nothing but a 1px gutter and row space - Dave's word was 'lets... try', so it lands as a specimen for his eye.
