  ▸ s217-D5 — RULED BENTO TYPES AND THE OPTION MATRIX — DISPLAY / GALLERY / DASHBOARD, EACH WITH RULED OPTION SETS; REFINES s217-D3 (ROLES RENAMED TO TYPES, GALLERY SQUARING BECOMES A PER-INSTANCE OPTION) (2026-08-23, Dave): The bento system lives in the showroom's Foundations/Layout section as a MATRIX of options over three TYPES (renaming s217-D3's roles; brochureware becomes DISPLAY). Background selectors exist for page background and bento background. DISPLAY: spacing tight/standard/generous = 1px/24px/40px; console tile radii as standard; keylines on/off; tight has no keylines by default - the bento or page background shows through the 1px gap. GALLERY: same three spacings; keylines on/off; caption background colour on/off; tight as per Display; mode is 'Justified rows' OR 'Gallery bento', the bento mode carrying a sub-option ragged or square bottom (this turns s217-D3's gallery squaring exemption into a per-instance choice); console image rounding options - '4 corners of image' or the full capsule of caption + image; backgrounds for page, bento and captions have two colour options - the lightest grey and white (dark-mode equivalents) - with the constraint that white captions require a grey ground and the inverse, and a third option, transparent. DASHBOARD: main layout bento spacing standard/generous only, NEVER tight; console keeps the established container-rounding rules on groupings; keylines on/off; sub-bentos have all three spacing options. OPEN POINTS, surfaced by the conductor and NOT resolved by this ruling: (1) tight+keylines-on proposed as flush tiles with hairline separators (inset-group pattern) since 1px cannot hold gap and line; (2) the caption inversion rule read as judged against the caption's immediate ground, transparent always legal; (3) capsule rounding proposed to require caption background or keylines; (4) console tile radius at tight spacing may pinch - a stepped-down radius shown as an alternative; (5) the grey/white/transparent palette applied to Display and Dashboard selectors by extension, proposed. Dave: 'lets see this for now. this is a lot, you might want to check my logic'.
