  ▸ s219-D3 — RULED ONE VOCABULARY, THREE PERMISSION LEVELS: GENERATION SHIPS DEFAULTS, EDIT PICKS WITHIN THE RAILS, AUTHORING WIDENS THEM; OPTIONS COME IN CHORDS; PAGEBG LEAVES THE BENTO GRAMMAR AND BENTOBG IS THE SECTION GROUND (2026-08-25, Dave): Ruled off Dave's #219 goal-setting message and his confirmation 'This sounds right'. (1) THREE DECISION POINTS, ONE VOCABULARY: generation, editing and authoring are permission levels on the same rails manifest, not systems. GENERATION ships the minted defaults only - zero decisions up front, every generated instance lands on canon ('probably the neatest way', his words); a future generation-time hint is an edit decision answered early, same vocabulary. EDITING picks within the rails and cannot leave canon. AUTHORING (designer-led build) is the only mode that widens the rails - a new option/chord runs the gates and its promotion into the manifest is a governance act (derivation governance, one level up). (2) OPTIONS COME IN CHORDS, NOT FREE DIALS: a chord settles several dials as a coherent set, ink follows ground automatically and is contrast-gated; the manifest carries a constraint layer - legal chords plus exclusion rules per theme x type intersection - and the validator refuses illegal combinations. Dave: 'some decisions might exclude others.' (3) THE FIRST TWO RULED CHORDS, from his console example, SCOPE CONSOLE GALLERY: chord one - full capsule + caption ground from the grey ramp INCLUDING dark grey with reversed-out text (the s219-D2(1)-retired DEFAULT returns as an OPTION, which is s219-D1's default-vs-option split working); chord two - four rounded corners on images + transparent caption background. Mono's access to the dark-caption chord is EXPRESSLY OPEN, not ruled. (4) PAGEBG LEAVES THE BENTO GRAMMAR: page background is a page-level general designer decision with its own small rail (white or the light greys in light mode; dark equivalents to be derived from tokens). (5) BENTOBG IS THE SECTION BACKGROUND DECISION: it stays in the grammar, may take any of the light or dark greys, and caption/ink contrast is measured against the EFFECTIVE ground. (6) THE LIBRARY SURFACES THE FULL EDIT-MODE OPTION SPACE, GENERATED FROM THE RAILS MANIFEST - library, editor and generator read one generated file so none can drift. (7) PROJECT TYPES (brochureware, products, web software, mobile apps) are a THIRD AXIS above theme x type - named, expressly PARKED.
