  ▸ s268-D4 — RULED AN UNRECEIVED RELEASE MAY BE RE-CUT AT THE SAME VERSION. 'Received' means handed to anyone outside the repo - the designers, a demo audience. A re-cut of an UNRECEIVED version records 're-cut' in the dist record and in the changelog, with BOTH shas (the superseded one and the new one), so the move is declared rather than silent. A RECEIVED release still bumps: the s257 laundering rule is unchanged for anything that has left the repo, and _gate_frozen_release.py still refuses RE-RECORDED WITHOUT A VERSION BUMP for those. Designer-facing packs: v1.0.6 was the last received; v1.0.13 is the next designer pack; bumps 7-12 stay as internal history. The register of what has been received is knowledge/_received.json - a version absent from it is unreceived, and the laundering arm's same-version clause is lifted for exactly those. (2026-09-11, Dave): Dave, chat, 2026-09-11: "lets apply this logic from now on" - applying, verbatim, the proposal put to him: "A release no one outside the repo has received may be re-cut at the same version; the dist record and changelog say 're-cut' with both shas. Bumps 7-12 stay as history; 12 becomes the one that goes to the designers."
      status: ENACTED (back-stamped #304 2026-09-26, Run 2 audit) in commit a4f78ee8 — basis MANUAL (hand-read receipt). Receipt: knowledge/_received.json:3 'THE RECEIVED REGISTER — s268-D4 …' introduced by a4f78ee8 'unreceived releases may be re-cut at version' · Was: 'ruled'. Audit record: notes/_lanes/304/R2/decisions.json
      ⚠ A RE-CUT IS NOT A SILENT RE-BAKE. The permission is to reuse the NUMBER, never to move a zip quietly: dist record and changelog must both say 're-cut' and carry both shas. And the received/unreceived question is answered by knowledge/_received.json, never by memory - if a version is in that register the old rule stands and you BUMP.
