  ▸ s268-D5 — RULED THE FOUR UNSEATED EDGE-TYPE KEYS ARE MINTED. Dave's word on lane E's RSQ 3 (lane C's RSQ 3, same content) is "mint all four": `composedOf`, `delegatesTo`, `drivesConsumer` and `$contract` get a SEAT in knowledge/components/meta.schema.json under `edges.properties`, with the semantics the corpus already carries and no more. composedOf / delegatesTo / drivesConsumer are arrays of the standard {ref, $note} edge; delegatesTo and drivesConsumer additionally carry an optional `when` string (the trigger, and the condition under which a consumer is driven), so `when` is added to the shared edge definition as an optional property named to those two types. `$contract` is a $-PREFIXED ANNOTATION, not an edge list: a free-form object holding the s263-D4 / s258-D1 marker contract the drivesConsumer edges are drawn from - it carries no refs and is therefore resolved against no registry. _validate_kg.py check (d) is taught the one distinction it lacked: a schema-declared $-prefixed key inside `edges` is an annotation and is not required to be an array of edges. Nothing beyond what filter-toolbar-bar.meta.json already states is minted - the seats describe the authored content, they do not extend it. (2026-09-11, Dave): Dave, chat, 2026-09-11: "mint all four" - in answer to lane E's RSQ 3, the four filter-toolbar-bar edge-type keys with no seat in the meta schema.
