  ▸ s268-D6 — RULED AUTHORED EDGES SURVIVE A REGENERATION, BY BOTH MECHANISMS AT ONCE. Dave's word on lane E's RSQ 2 is "both now" - option (a) NOW and option (c) NOW, not (c) later. Read back and confirmed 2026-09-11: "yes both now plaease" (verbatim). (a) DECLARED_EDGE_TYPES in knowledge/gen_kg_edges.py is widened from its single entry ("groupsWith") to EVERY schema-legal edge type the generator does not derive from prose: composedOf, delegatesTo, drivesConsumer, $contract, groupsWith. Authored is now the DEFAULT for any type the generator has no prose source for. (c) The generator NEVER WIPES `edges` again. It reads the meta's existing edges, refreshes only the types it actually derives, and leaves every other type untouched; within a derived type it matches each generated edge against the existing ones (exact $note, then ref, then hasPart part-name, then either-way $note prefix) and KEEPS the authored entry - refreshing only its `ref` - so a hand-extended $note is not truncated by a regeneration. Unmatched generated edges are appended; nothing is deleted. The splice is IN PLACE, so a meta whose edges did not change is byte-identical after a run. Because carried edges may reference registry nodes the derivation no longer mints, the two node registries carry those entries forward verbatim from their own previous content rather than dropping a live-referenced node. s245-D7's carry mechanism is unchanged in kind: this widens it, and makes the loss structurally impossible rather than list-dependent. (2026-09-11, Dave): Dave, chat, 2026-09-11: "both now (a) now - widen DECLARED_EDGE_TYPES to every schema-legal type the generator doesn't derive; (c) later - generator never wipes edges, only refreshes derived types." - in answer to lane E's RSQ 2.
      status: ENACTED (back-stamped #304 2026-09-26, Run 2 audit) in commit 03e519cb — basis S-A (commit body names it with an enactment verb and touches a governed file). Receipt: commit 03e519cb (2026-09-11) touching knowledge/gen_kg_edges.py: 's268-D6 enacted (a)+(c): DECLARED_EDGE_TYPES widened off the schema, generator never wipes edges (per-edge refresh, in-place splice, registry carry), hasPart PROMOTE joined on the part name not the mutable use prose' · Was: 'ruled'. Audit record: notes/_lanes/304/R2/decisions.json
