  ▸ s278-D1 — RULED THE THIN SLICE IS A SEED, AND ASK IS THE ON-DEMAND DOOR — the s277-D13 clause, ruled. The slice is COMPOSED ONCE at step 1 by `_compose_slice.py` and the session then works from its own state; it is a seed, not persistent session state and not a live projection of the graph. ASK (s277-D13's typed-question door) is the ON-DEMAND half: it is called mid-session whenever the designer's next prompt needs a node the seed excluded, and it READS THE CONSTITUTION LIVE — so a ruling inscribed after the seed was composed is answerable through ASK without recomposing. Seed and on-demand door under one contract; neither replaces the other. This ruling CLOSES the open clause s277-D13 recorded as a question and inscribes no new mechanism beyond it. (2026-09-16, Dave): on the read-back of the s277-D13 clause at #278: 'Ill go with you, lets just move on to the other graph work'
