  ▸ s282-D2 — RULED THE RED-TEXT BAN IS ON THE PRIMARY HSBC RED; THE EXCEPTION IS A SECONDARY RED ONLY. col26-016's stored sentence is correct insomuch as it applies to the primary red. The stat-card exception s282-D1 added (RAG red down, RAG green up) is for a SECONDARY red - usually the RAG/delta red (`data/delta/loss`) - and never the primary. His claim that one or two themes carry a readable secondary red is recorded VERBATIM in the guideline and is UNPROVEN against the live token set (no such token exists today); it is his word, not a token, until a theme mints one. col26-012 (chart red) is NOT edited: its scoped-override cross-reference to dv-019 already stands in the file (lines 79-81) and his 'cross-reference' is thereby satisfied - the ASK is CLOSED, not enacted. (2026-09-17, Dave): chat #282 2026-09-17, on the col26-012 ASK and the col26-016 exception: 'cross-reference but this rule about red text isn't as precise as it should be, the original rule is correct insomuch as it applies to the primary red, the red text exception is only for a secondary red usually the rag red, I think we have RAG red and a readable secondary red for 1 or two of the themes.'
