  ▸ s282-D3 — RULED LOGO SIZE IS MEASURED BY HEIGHT, ON A FIVE-STEP SCALE: x-small 24 · small 28 · medium 32 · large 36 · x-large 40 px (CORRECTED BY DAVE THE SAME MORNING from 32/36/40/48/56 - 'I think I got the scale wrong now I'm looking at it'; the first figures stood for one commit, 0acb019, and are superseded here, not deleted). THE HEIGHT IS THE RAW HEIGHT OF THE ARTWORK, NOT A VIEWBOX SCALED TO IT - his 'no view boxes, just the raw height' and 'and width obviously': a shipped logo asset at a step carries its raw pixel height AND width as its own coordinates, so its edges can sit on the pixel grid; the review sheet still scales the one Figma export through a viewBox because no per-size masters exist yet, and that is the gap a masters lane closes. Width follows the lockup's own ratio and is never the measure. This supersedes the WIDTH framing the #282 logo-review page shipped with (120 / 64 / minimum) and reframes va25-014's 105x20px digital minimum, which is a width figure from the 2025 standard: it sits BELOW x-small and is not contradicted, but whether any lockup may render UNDER x-small (24px high) is NOT ruled here. Clear space is NOT ruled here. The sheet on notes/_lanes/282/logo-review/LOGO-REVIEW-2026-09-17.html is re-rendered at the five heights; a logo size token set, if minted, takes these five names and values. At phone width the 795:85 identifier lockup cannot hold medium and above inside a 16px gutter and is allowed to shrink there — measured 28px at 390 for medium, large and x-large — a rendering fact, not a step. (2026-09-18, Dave): chat #282 2026-09-18: 'height is the right measurement here, go from 32 -36 - 40 - 48 - 56 x-small, small, medium, large, x-large,' · then: 'I think I got the scale wrong now I'm looking at it. 24, 28, 32, 36, 40' · then: 'no view boxes, just the raw height' · 'and width obviously'
