  ▸ s282-D4 — RULED THE MASTERBRAND-WITH-IDENTIFIER LOCKUP IS SCRAPPED. The logo set is TWO lockups - hexagon and masterbrand - x colour/mono x on-light/on-dark = 8 variants, not 12. The four identifier files are moved on disk to _to_delete/logos-identifier-282/ (a gitignored holding dir: the mount refuses unlink) and REMOVED from the tracked tree - git history at c143a1b keeps them, their four logo: nodes and four governedBy-null edges leave _logo_nodes.json by regeneration (gen_kg_icons.py --land --ratified s277-D4: 12 -> 8 nodes, 31 -> 27 edges, nothing else changed), logos.md says two lockups, and the #282 logo-review page's identifier sections and the three identifier defect questions (q1-colour, q1-mono, q1-light-mono) are struck as moot, kept on the sheet as the record of what was reviewed. The two BLOCKING exporter defects the review found were both identifier files, so they close with this; the hexagon duplicate pair and the four unreferenced hexagons remain the review's live questions. (2026-09-18, Dave): chat #282 2026-09-18: 'scrap the identifier versions'
