  ▸ s308-D34 — RULED EDGE QUESTIONS, CALL 1: A CAROUSEL HOLDS CARDS — THE WORKING CONTAINMENT, UNTIL CARDS AND TILES ARE DEFINED. Dave chose, verbatim: 'A · A carousel holds cards' (the recommendation), with his note, verbatim in full: 'i think we have to create a definition for cards and tiles, this might help as a differentiator, in the case of a bento one of it's 'tiles' could contain a carousel, it's tricky as a card is a container and a carousel can sit in a container, is the question about the hierarchy of containers or clear definitions for different types. we need to work this out, is there a standard nomenclature for this?'. So: cards stay containedBy carousel, and carousel's livesInside line 'Cards (a media card sequence)' and the containedBy edge it made are removed; the carousel/cards containment loop is gone. A STANDS ONLY UNTIL THE CARD / TILE DEFINITIONS LAND: his note opens a definitions question (cards versus tiles; a bento tile that can hold a carousel; whether this is about the hierarchy of containers or about clear definitions for types; whether a standard nomenclature exists), which goes to a separate research lane, and A may then be re-expressed as type-based 'accepts' rules (what a container type accepts) instead of a component-to-component containment line. (2026-09-29, Dave): review page export, Tue 2026-09-29 17:07 BST (notes/_REVIEW-308-edge-questions-2026-09-29-v1.html, 'Copy as text' headed 'Session 308 · edge questions · answers', pasted into chat #308, saved verbatim as notes/_lanes/308/DAVE-RULINGS-2026-09-29-1708-drift-and-edges.md § Edge questions) · he took all five recommendations · call 1, verbatim: 'Chose: A · A carousel holds cards (the recommendation)' · 'In his words: i think we have to create a definition for cards and tiles, this might help as a differentiator, in the case of a bento one of it's 'tiles' could contain a carousel, it's tricky as a card is a container and a carousel can sit in a container, is the question abou