  ▸ s309-D1 — RULED THE CONDUCTOR'S CALL ON THE KIND OF TABS, ACCORDION AND POPOVER IS ANSWERED IN CHAT: GOOD - TABS, ACCORDION AND POPOVER ARE BLOCKS, NOT HOUSINGS. They fold or reveal content inside whatever holds them; a housing is a surfaced thing placed in a layout. Lane B of #309 had classed the three as housings (s308-D44's definition), which made the advisory accepts check refuse 5 containedBy lines on the real tree (tabs, accordion and popover inside Cards as CARD-HOLDS; popover holding table and summary as NOT-ACCEPTED). Dave's answer, in chat, verbatim: 'good', to the conductor's call 1, verbatim: 'Tabs, accordion and popover are blocks, not housings. I'd take it: they fold or reveal content inside whatever holds them, where a housing is a surfaced thing placed in a layout — and it keeps your card rule whole.'. RECORD: the three metas take kind `block`; the accepts check in `_validate_edges.py --check` is expected to read 0 refusals on the real tree; W-308is's seam control becomes clean. (2026-09-29, Dave): chat #309, Tue 2026-09-29 21:37 BST, saved verbatim as notes/_lanes/309/DAVE-WORDS-2026-09-29-2137.md · the conductor's call 1 (21:35 BST), verbatim: 'Tabs, accordion and popover are blocks, not housings. I'd take it: they fold or reveal content inside whatever holds them, where a housing is a surfaced thing placed in a layout — and it keeps your card rule whole.' — his answer, in chat, verbatim: '1. good'
