  ▸ s311-D4 — RULED THE NEUTRAL SPEC LIVES IN THE META, as four new fields in knowledge/components/meta.schema.json: anatomy (an element tree naming parts, slots, aria and the attributes each state sets, prop holes as '{props.x}', state attributes as '{state.y}'), states (states, initial, transitions {from,on,to,guard?} and the keyboard map, Zag-shaped), emits (the events a part fires, with payload types; behaviour.events stays as the listener list beside it), and bindings (the snippet's #token-manifest moved in as DTCG references, replacing the 727 prose token entries). No separate spec file per component, no third-party source format (Mitosis or Stencil). Phase 1 adds the four fields and renames none; the #252-#276 meta work (provides, when, accepts, the #253 tags) is kept. Dave, by click, verbatim: 'In the meta: four new fields' (the recommendation); comment: none. (2026-10-01, Dave): proposal page export, Thu 2026-10-01 11:10 BST ('Copy as text' pasted into chat #311; notes/_PROPOSAL-311-apollo-for-other-libraries-2026-10-01-v1.html, saved verbatim as notes/_lanes/311/DAVE-RULINGS-2026-10-01-1110-apollo-for-other-libraries.md) · call 2, verbatim: 'Where the spec lives' — his answer, by click, verbatim: 'In the meta: four new fields (the recommendation)' · comment: none · page note, verbatim: 'This cool, lets get it done' · his chat line after the export, verbatim: 'How do we role this into our other plans, this probably needs revising'
